(Mini AI Knowledge Assistant - Sample Document) Tj
T*
T*
(Section 1: What is Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\)?) Tj
T*
(Retrieval-Augmented Generation, commonly known as RAG, is an artificial intelligence framework) Tj
T*
(designed to improve the quality of large language model responses by grounding the model on) Tj
T*
(external knowledge sources. While standard language models are trained on large corpuses of data,) Tj
T*
(their knowledge is static and cut off at their training date. Furthermore, models can generate) Tj
T*
(factually incorrect information, a phenomenon known as hallucination.) Tj
T*
T*
(RAG addresses these challenges by retrieving authoritative facts from an external knowledge base) Tj
T*
(before generating a response. This allows the model to reference timely and private data,) Tj
T*
(substantially reducing the likelihood of hallucinations.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
