(Section 2: The Core RAG Pipeline) Tj
T*
(The architecture of a typical RAG system consists of three fundamental stages:) Tj
T*
(1. Ingestion: Documents such as PDFs or text files are parsed, cleaned, and split into smaller) Tj
T*
(manageable segments called text chunks.) Tj
T*
(2. Indexing: Each chunk is passed through an embedding model to produce a high-dimensional vector) Tj
T*
(representation. These vectors are stored in a vector database such as FAISS or Chroma.) Tj
T*
(3. Retrieval and Generation: When a user poses a question, the query is converted into an embedding.) Tj
T*
(The vector database performs a cosine similarity search to find the most relevant chunks.) Tj
T*
(Finally, the retrieved chunks and the user query are assembled into a prompt and submitted to an LLM.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
