(Section 3: Chunking Strategies and Grounded Answering) Tj
T*
(Chunking is the process of breaking long documents into cohesive, smaller units. Two primary) Tj
T*
(parameters govern chunking: chunk size and chunk overlap. Chunk size determines the maximum length) Tj
T*
(of each fragment, while chunk overlap ensures that context spanning chunk boundaries is not lost.) Tj
T*
T*
(To guarantee grounded answers, the system prompt must explicitly instruct the LLM to answer only) Tj
T*
(using the retrieved facts. If the information is missing from the context, the assistant must) Tj
T*
(state that it cannot find the answer rather than speculating.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
